WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.360
A small-town bakery owes 100
dollars a day for its ovens,

2
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.510
even on days it bakes nothing.

3
00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:08.850
Early batches get cheaper to make.

4
00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:12.580
The 3rd batch adds only
30 dollars to its costs.

5
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:14.810
Then something flips.

6
00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:17.060
The 5th batch adds 80 dollars.

7
00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.840
The 6th adds 120.

8
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.250
Why can the next batch
of bread cost a bakery

9
00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.110
more to make than the batches before it?

10
00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:27.390
In this mission, you'll calculate fixed,

11
00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:30.390
variable, average and marginal cost,

12
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.060
then draw the curves.

13
00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:34.350
Then you'll hit the
bakery with a rent hike

14
00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:38.040
and a wage raise, and
predict which curves shift.

15
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.980
Your mission: find out
what pushes up the cost

16
00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.190
of the next batch.
